cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use MEWracle in academic work, please cite it as below."
title: MEWracle
abstract: >-
  The open-source platform for designing melt electrowriting (MEW) scaffolds
  and modelling how they print, for any MEW printer. It designs scaffolds on a
  flat collector or a rotating mandrel, writes the G-code, and models where
  every fiber lands: fiber diameter, jet lag, coiling below the critical
  speed, sagging between the fibers that hold a fiber up, and fusion into the
  layer below. Each model can be calibrated to the user's printer and polymer.
type: software
version: 1.0.0-beta
authors:
  - family-names: Harris
    given-names: Joseph
    affiliation: >-
      University of Oregon (work performed during an internship at Ohio State
      University)
repository-code: "https://github.com/umpquajoseph/MEWracle"
license: AGPL-3.0-only
keywords:
  - melt electrowriting
  - scaffold design
  - G-code
  - physical modelling
